Completion
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

FIXME(mundane): The crew finishes the pylon. Veran checks the cable connections one by one. Chorik fits the top cross-piece. Baret rolls up the rest circle and stows the kit. Richard reads the activation sequence from a laminated card he keeps in his pocket. Twenty minutes of focused work. The four of them work the way the crew of any well-run job works. When the last bolt is tight Richard turns the key on the housing.

FIXME(dread): There is a click. Something cycles up inside the housing. The pylon is live.

FIXME(revelation): The weight is immediate. It is not pain. It is purpose. Blueprints unroll in your mind: schematics with part numbers for components you have never seen and now understand the function of, coordinates for the next site east, material quantities, scheduling margins. The full weight of a job that is organized and waiting and makes complete sense.

FIXME(revelation): You push against it. The signal does not feel hostile. It feels like an offer. You push against it because you know what it is.

FIXME(dread): You surface. The crew is somewhere else behind the eyes. They are present in body. They are not coordinated yet. The activator housing is at the base of the pylon, closed and latched. The window will not stay open.

# GAP (load-bearing): the bibles called for a save-shaped resist roll
# here with Cunning as the default skill. Deferred from the skeleton
# pending author decision on the signal_caught fragment quality. If
# the author wants it, drop a single picker choice between the body
# and the act/walk choices below, with both branches +open-ing into a
# small Window.enc file that hosts the act/walk fork.

choices:

* Move on the housing = Try to break the activator before the crew firms up
    FIXME(action): You move. The housing is small and bolted to the bedrock. You have to find the seam where the bolts seat into the metal. The crew is starting to turn.
    @if check cunning correct:scheme wrong:bluff {
        FIXME(action): You read the seam fast. You drive the heel of your hand against the latch plate. The plate bends. You strip the housing open and pull the activator unit out and break it across your knee. The signal cuts. The pylon goes dark behind you.
        +open "Aftermath"
    } @else {
        FIXME(action): You go at the housing without reading it first. The latch plate does not give. Before you can try again Veran has a hand on your shoulder. He is not aggressive. He is firm.
        +open "Grabbed"
    }

* Let the window close = Stay where you are
    FIXME(dread): You do not move. The window closes. The crew finishes their transition. They collect their tools with the synchronized economy of people who know exactly where they are going and why. The pylon hums behind them as they head east down the mesa road. They do not look back.
    FIXME(dread): You are alone on the mesa with it. The coordinates for the next site are still in your head, whether you want them or not.
    +finish_dungeon
    +add_level
